IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `au-interpretation-time`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (Australia): PART 4, Amendment, repeal and expiry of Acts
-- (ss 7 to 11B). What a repeal or amendment does to things done, rights and liabilities
-- under the repealed or amended text: s 7. Revival: s 7(1). Re-enactment: ss 10 and 10A.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. The whole of Part 4 is "subject to a contrary
-- intention" (s 2(2)); whether one appears is an INPUT, never guessed.
-- Sections 8, 8A, 8B, 8C and 9 are repealed (endnote 4: "rep No 46, 2011").

§ `Part 4: Amendment, repeal and expiry of Acts`

§§ `Section 7: effect of repeal or amendment of an Act`

DECLARE `Way a repeal or amendment may occur` IS ONE OF
    `an express repeal or amendment`
    `a repeal or amendment effected by implication`
    `the expiry, lapsing or cessation of effect of the Act or part`
    `the abrogation or limitation of the effect of the Act or part`
    `the exclusion of the application of the Act or part to any person, subject-matter or circumstance`

DECLARE `Kind of thing the repeal or amendment may touch` IS ONE OF
    `something not in force or existing when the repeal or amendment takes effect`
    `the previous operation of the affected Act or part, or anything duly done or suffered under it`
    `a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it`
    `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of an offence committed against it`
    `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture or punishment`

DECLARE `What becomes of the thing` IS ONE OF
    `it is not revived`
    `it is left as it was, as if the affected Act or part had not been repealed or amended`
    `section 7(2) gives no answer because a contrary intention appears`

-- 7(1): no revival of the old Act or part when the Act or part that repealed it is itself
-- repealed, unless express provision is made for the revival.
-- src:262 | No revival of other Act or part
-- src:263 | (1) The repeal of an Act, or of a part of an Act, that repealed an Act (the old Act) or part (the old part) of an Act does not revive the old Act or old part, unless express provision is made for the revival.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 7(1) (src:262-263)
GIVEN `express provision is made for the revival` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the repeal of the repealing Act or part revives the old Act or part` `express provision is made for the revival` MEANS
    `express provision is made for the revival`

-- 7(2): a repeal or amendment, by an Act or by an instrument under an Act, does not (a)
-- revive anything not in force or existing at the time it takes effect, or (b) to (e)
-- affect what is listed; an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy may be instituted,
-- continued or enforced, and a penalty imposed, as if the affected Act or part had not
-- been repealed or amended.
-- src:264 | No effect on previous operation of Act or part
-- src:265 | (2) If an Act, or an instrument under an Act, repeals or amends an Act (the affected Act) or a part of an Act, then the repeal or amendment does not:
-- src:266 | (a) revive anything not in force or existing at the time at which the repeal or amendment takes effect; or
-- src:267 | (b) affect the previous operation of the affected Act or part (including any amendment made by the affected Act or part), or anything duly done or suffered under the affected Act or part; or
-- src:268 | (c) affect any right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the affected Act or part; or
-- src:269 | (d) affect any penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of any offence committed against the affected Act or part; or
-- src:270 | (e) affect any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of any such right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture or punishment.
-- src:271 | Any such investigation, legal proceeding or remedy may be instituted, continued or enforced, and any such penalty, forfeiture or punishment may be imposed, as if the affected Act or part had not been repealed or amended.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 7(2) (src:264-271)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of thing the repeal or amendment may touch`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What becomes of the thing`
`what a repeal or amendment does to` kind `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF   `a contrary intention appears`
    THEN `section 7(2) gives no answer because a contrary intention appears`
    ELSE CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `something not in force or existing when the repeal or amendment takes effect`
              THEN `it is not revived`
         WHEN `the previous operation of the affected Act or part, or anything duly done or suffered under it`
              THEN `it is left as it was, as if the affected Act or part had not been repealed or amended`
         WHEN `a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it`
              THEN `it is left as it was, as if the affected Act or part had not been repealed or amended`
         WHEN `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of an offence committed against it`
              THEN `it is left as it was, as if the affected Act or part had not been repealed or amended`
         WHEN `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture or punishment`
              THEN `it is left as it was, as if the affected Act or part had not been repealed or amended`

-- 7(3): "repeal or amendment" in 7(1) and (2) includes all five ways. 7(4): "a part of an Act"
-- includes any provision of, or words, figures, drawings or symbols in, an Act.
-- src:273 | Interpretation
-- src:274 | (3) A reference in subsection (1) or (2) to the repeal or amendment of an Act or of a part of an Act includes a reference to:
-- src:275 | (a) a repeal or amendment effected by implication; and
-- src:276 | (b) the expiry, lapsing or cessation of effect of the Act or part; and
-- src:277 | (c) the abrogation or limitation of the effect of the Act or part; and
-- src:278 | (d) the exclusion of the application of the Act or part to any person, subject-matter or circumstance.
-- src:279 | (4) A reference in this section to a part of an Act includes a reference to any provision of, or words, figures, drawings or symbols in, an Act.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 7(3) and (4) (src:273-279)
GIVEN way IS A `Way a repeal or amendment may occur`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`counts as a repeal or amendment for section 7` way MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `an express repeal or amendment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a repeal or amendment effected by implication` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the expiry, lapsing or cessation of effect of the Act or part` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the abrogation or limitation of the effect of the Act or part` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the exclusion of the application of the Act or part to any person, subject-matter or circumstance` THEN TRUE

§§ `Sections 10 and 10A: references to amended or re-enacted laws`

-- 10(a): a reference to the short title of another Act is a reference to that Act as
-- originally enacted and as amended from time to time.
-- src:280 | 10 References to amended or re-enacted Acts
-- src:281 | Where an Act contains a reference to a short title that is or was provided by law for the citation of another Act as originally enacted, or of another Act as amended, then:
-- src:282 | (a) the reference shall be construed as a reference to that other Act as originally enacted and as amended from time to time; and
-- src:283 | (b) where that other Act has been repealed and re-enacted, with or without modifications, the reference shall be construed as including a reference to the re-enacted Act as originally enacted and as amended from time to time; and
-- src:284 | (c) if a provision of the other Act is repealed and re-enacted (including where the other Act is repealed and re-enacted), with or without modifications, a reference to the repealed provision extends to any corresponding re-enacted provision (whether or not the re-enacted provision has the same number as the repealed provision).
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 10 (src:280-284)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a reference to the short title of another Act includes that Act as amended from time to time` MEANS TRUE

-- 10(b): if that other Act has been repealed and re-enacted, with or without
-- modifications, the reference includes the re-enacted Act.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 10(b) (src:283)
GIVEN `the other Act has been repealed and re-enacted, with or without modifications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the reference includes the re-enacted Act` `the other Act has been repealed and re-enacted, with or without modifications` MEANS
    `the other Act has been repealed and re-enacted, with or without modifications`

-- 10(c): if a provision of the other Act is repealed and re-enacted, a reference to the
-- repealed provision extends to any corresponding re-enacted provision, whether or not
-- the re-enacted provision has the same number as the repealed one (so the number is
-- not a parameter).
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 10(c) (src:284)
GIVEN `the provision has been repealed and re-enacted, with or without modifications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the re-enacted provision corresponds to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the reference to the repealed provision extends to the re-enacted provision` `the provision has been repealed and re-enacted, with or without modifications` `the re-enacted provision corresponds to it` MEANS
    `the provision has been repealed and re-enacted, with or without modifications` AND `the re-enacted provision corresponds to it`

-- 10A is the same rule for a short title or other citation of a law of a State or Territory
-- ("re-enacted or re-made").
-- src:285 | 10A References to amended or re-enacted laws of States and Territories
-- src:286 | Where an Act contains a reference to a short title or other citation that is or was provided by the law of a State or Territory for the citation of a law of that State or Territory as originally enacted or made, or as amended, then:
-- src:287 | (a) the reference shall be construed as a reference to that law as originally enacted or made and as amended from time to time; and
-- src:288 | (b) where that law has been repealed and re-enacted or re-made, with or without modifications, the reference shall be construed as including a reference to the re-enacted or re-made law as originally enacted or made and as amended from time to time; and
-- src:289 | (c) if a provision of that law is repealed and re-enacted or re-made (including where that law is repealed and re-enacted or re-made), with or without modifications, a reference to the repealed provision extends to any corresponding re-enacted or re-made provision (whether or not the re-enacted or re-made provision has the same number as the repealed provision).
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 10A (src:285-289)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a reference to a citation of a law of a State or Territory includes that law as originally enacted or made and as amended from time to time` MEANS TRUE

@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 10A(b) (src:288)
GIVEN `the law has been repealed and re-enacted or re-made, with or without modifications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the reference includes the re-enacted or re-made law` `the law has been repealed and re-enacted or re-made, with or without modifications` MEANS
    `the law has been repealed and re-enacted or re-made, with or without modifications`

@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 10A(c) (src:289)
GIVEN `the provision has been repealed and re-enacted or re-made, with or without modifications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the re-enacted or re-made provision corresponds to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the reference to the repealed provision of the State or Territory law extends to the re-enacted or re-made provision` `the provision has been repealed and re-enacted or re-made, with or without modifications` `the re-enacted or re-made provision corresponds to it` MEANS
    `the provision has been repealed and re-enacted or re-made, with or without modifications` AND `the re-enacted or re-made provision corresponds to it`

§§ `Sections 11 and 11B`

-- src:290 | 11 Acts may be altered etc. in same session
-- src:291 | An Act may be altered, amended or repealed in the same session of Parliament in which it was passed.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 11 (src:290-291)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an Act may be altered, amended or repealed in the same session of Parliament in which it was passed` MEANS TRUE

-- src:300 | 11B Amending Act to be construed with amended Act
-- src:301 | (1) Every Act amending another Act must be construed with the other Act as part of the other Act.
-- src:302 | (2) If:
-- src:303 | (a) an Act (the amending Act) amends another Act (the principal Act); and
-- src:304 | (b) a provision (the non-amending provision) of the amending Act does not amend the principal Act, but relates to an amendment of the principal Act made by another provision of the amending Act; and
-- src:305 | (c) a term is used in the non-amending provision that has a particular meaning in the principal Act or in a provision of the principal Act amended or included by the amending Act;
-- src:306 | then the term has that meaning in the non-amending provision.
-- src:307 | Note: Subsection (2) covers, for example, application, transitional and saving items in a Schedule to an amending Act that relate to amendments of a principal Act made by other items in the Schedule.
-- src:308 | (3) Subsection (2) does not limit subsection (1).
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 11B(1) to (3) (src:300-308)
GIVEN `the amending Act amends the principal Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision does not amend the principal Act but relates to an amendment of it made by another provision of the amending Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term has a particular meaning in the principal Act or in a provision of it amended or included by the amending Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the term has that meaning in the non-amending provision` `the amending Act amends the principal Act` `the provision does not amend the principal Act but relates to an amendment of it made by another provision of the amending Act` `the term has a particular meaning in the principal Act or in a provision of it amended or included by the amending Act` MEANS
        `the amending Act amends the principal Act`
    AND `the provision does not amend the principal Act but relates to an amendment of it made by another provision of the amending Act`
    AND `the term has a particular meaning in the principal Act or in a provision of it amended or included by the amending Act`
